From e5c4514486a048c685437f5b8273abccd444a01a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:24:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(flash-next): read PLE history from the fork source during
 prefill

A prefill that continues a StateImage fork (after a context-cache capture inside
the prompt) has distinct source and destination slots. The GDN layers read the
source and write the destination, but prefill PLE updated the destination slot
in place, so layer 1 consumed whatever PLE history that slot last held instead
of the checkpoint's. Output then depended on slot reuse, and so on
max_concurrency.

flash_next_ple now takes source and destination history, which may alias, and
the prefill schedule passes both slots. The op test also covers the fork form.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PB8TNZ3p817zVAp6aH4yrz
